1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,542
The market fell 56%. Netflix rose 66%.

2
00:00:03,543 --> 00:00:07,466
One line on the chart flagged it early.

3
00:00:07,467 --> 00:00:13,066
That line is relative strength: Netflix's price divided by the S&P 500.

4
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:18,666
It rises when Netflix beats the market. It falls when it lags.

5
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:22,399
Late 2008. Stocks crashed. Netflix fell hard too.

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:26,132
Then it bounced back faster than the market.

7
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:31,179
In December 2008, the RS line hit a new 52-week high.

8
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:35,466
The price was still 35% below its own high.

9
00:00:35,467 --> 00:00:40,726
Fourteen weeks later, the price broke to a new high too.

10
00:00:40,727 --> 00:00:44,799
The market was still 52% below its peak.

11
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:49,170
From there, Netflix rose 176% in 15 months.

12
00:00:49,171 --> 00:00:52,266
The S&P 500 rose 36%.

13
00:00:52,267 --> 00:00:56,519
Leaders often show strength before their price does.

14
00:00:56,520 --> 00:01:01,599
It's a clue for your watchlist, not a buy signal.

15
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:07,149
Lore 011. Next: Lore 012, ADR% in 15 seconds
